{"duration_api_ms": 38446, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "468af5ef-cb71-4782-8196-54556a4a1c3a", "total_cost_usd": 0.010686455, "usage": {"input_tokens": 24, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 27871, "cache_read_input_tokens": 374768, "output_tokens": 6905, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 600}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 27871}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 754, "cache_read_input_tokens": 40486, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 299, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 299, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-5-5": {"inputTokens": 24, "outputTokens": 6905, "cacheReadInputTokens": 374768, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 27871, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.010686455, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 600, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-5-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 19, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`Table.transform()` and `Table.transform_sql()` now take `strict=`, and `sqlite-utils transform` has `--strict/--no-strict`. The acceptance check passes: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_transform.py tests/test_cli.py` gives 270 passed, 3 skipped. I did not commit anything.\n\nChanges, all as the spec describes:\n- **`sqlite_utils/db.py`**: the new parameter and docstring on `transform_sql` and `transform`. `transform_sql` raises `TransformError` for `strict=True` without STRICT support, and builds the new table with `self.strict if strict is None else strict`. `transform` stores a non-`None` value in `self._defaults[\"strict\"]` just before `return self`.\n- **`sqlite_utils/cli.py`**: the `--strict/--no-strict` option above `--sql`, with the `strict` parameter passed to both `transform_sql` and `transform`.\n- **`docs/python-api.rst`**: a \"Changing strict mode\" section with the `python_api_transform_strict` label, placed before the rename-columns label.\n- **`docs/cli.rst`**: `--strict` and `--no-strict` entries after `--add-foreign-key`.\n\nOn the rollback requirement: I did not change the transaction handling. The copy statement and the temporary table creation both run inside the existing `with self.db.atomic()` block, so a row that fails the strict check should roll back the whole change. I reasoned this from the code rather than writing a new test for it. The existing tests pass, but I did not check whether one of them covers the failing-row case.", "ttft_ms": 2138, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 49900, "uuid": "1c3e6c20-136a-4e86-a2eb-d8f2e0cb8cac", "ttft_stream_ms": 1856, "time_to_request_ms": 197, "first_content_frame_ms": 1856, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
